A||N||10||2xsess||What's the deal with EGR tubes||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||10-17-2000||06:13 PM||||I've seen the threads about EGR tubes going bad and I've been getting the imfamous code 32. What goes wrong with the tube? Does it crack? <P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-17-2000||06:27 PM||||Your  right...  they crack around or toward the intake end ...  I think...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||10-17-2000||06:27 PM||||Yes - on V6's at least, the tube that conveys exhaust gas from the EGR valve to the plenum frequently develops cracks and can cause idle speed to be too high.<P>Code 32, on the other hand, means the EGR solenoid isn't getting a vacuum signal from the plenum.  Cracked or disconnected vacuum line to the EGR solenoid can cause that.    ||||reg||3
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-17-2000||09:33 PM||||you can bypass the egr solenoid buy t-off the vaccuum line from the fuel canister (top line on the fire wall) and plumbing it in to the egr. worked on my 86SE to pass emissions.. and drive another 8+ months!<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||10-18-2000||05:21 PM||||Well, I found out the deal with them first hand today. I had the car running with the decklid open and I was just messing around under there. I moved the heat sleeve on my EGR tube and it hissed at me. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||10-18-2000||05:37 PM||||How rude of it!  The replacement tube is (was) about $100 at your GM dealer.  However, I believe it can be welded.  Aftermarket EGR tubes may be available, too - might try Rodney Dickman's page.  ||||reg||4
Z||000006||2xsess||10-18-2000||05:41 PM||||I thought that was very rude of it!!<BR>I'm going to check the one on the parts car that SDM and I are working on. I think IRM has replacement ones too. I'll check Rodney first though.<P>Just checked and Rodney doesn't have them. Maybe a thought for a future product for him though?<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||10-18-2000||08:20 PM||||FOCOA has them. Or at least had them.  Item #230 in the last issue of the "Fiero Owner" had  a flexible EGR tube $79.  New phone # 714-635-0898 for FOCOA.||||reg||1
